PAR1{"schema":{"fields":[{"name":"book_source","type":"string"},{"name":"chapter_name","type":"string"},{"name":"question_number_in_book","type":"int32"},{"name":"question_text","type":"string"},{"name":"options","type":"string"},{"name":"correct_option","type":"string"},{"name":"solution_text","type":"string"},{"name":"exam_metadata","type":"string"},{"name":"admin_tags","type":"string"}]},"compression":"snappy","rowCount":20,"created":"2025-09-16T17:08:58.727Z"}[{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Percentage","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"What is 20% of 100?","options":"{\"a\":\"10\",\"b\":\"20\",\"c\":\"30\",\"d\":\"40\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"$20\\%$ of $100 = \\dfrac{20}{100}\\times 100 = 20$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2023 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Percentage\",\"Basic Math\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Percentage","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"If the price of a commodity increases by 25%, by what percentage should it be reduced to bring it back to the original price?","options":"{\"a\":\"15%\",\"b\":\"20%\",\"c\":\"25%\",\"d\":\"30%\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Let original price be $100$. After 25% increase: $100 + 25 = 125$. To reduce to $100$: $\\dfrac{25}{125} \\times 100 = 20\\%$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Percentage\",\"Price Change\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Profit & Loss","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"A man buys a pen for ₹50 and sells it at a profit of 20%. Find the selling price.","options":"{\"a\":\"55\",\"b\":\"58\",\"c\":\"60\",\"d\":\"62\"}","correct_option":"c","solution_text":"Selling Price $= 50 + \\dfrac{20}{100}\\times 50 = 50 + 10 = 60$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Profit & Loss\",\"Profit Calculation\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Profit & Loss","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"A shopkeeper marks his goods 30% above cost price and gives a discount of 10%. What is his profit percentage?","options":"{\"a\":\"15%\",\"b\":\"17%\",\"c\":\"20%\",\"d\":\"23%\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Let CP = 100. MP = 130. SP = 130 - 10% of 130 = 130 - 13 = 117. Profit = 117 - 100 = 17. Profit% = $\\dfrac{17}{100} \\times 100 = 17\\%$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2021 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Profit & Loss\",\"Marked Price\",\"Discount\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Simple Interest","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"Find the simple interest on ₹1000 at 10% per annum for 2 years.","options":"{\"a\":\"150\",\"b\":\"180\",\"c\":\"200\",\"d\":\"220\"}","correct_option":"c","solution_text":"$SI = \\dfrac{P \\times R \\times T}{100} = \\dfrac{1000 \\times 10 \\times 2}{100} = 200$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2021 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Simple Interest\",\"Interest Calculation\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Simple Interest","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"At what rate of simple interest will ₹5000 amount to ₹6000 in 4 years?","options":"{\"a\":\"4%\",\"b\":\"5%\",\"c\":\"6%\",\"d\":\"8%\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"SI = 6000 - 5000 = 1000. $R = \\dfrac{SI \\times 100}{P \\times T} = \\dfrac{1000 \\times 100}{5000 \\times 4} = 5\\%$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2020 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Simple Interest\",\"Rate Calculation\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Compound Interest","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"Find the compound interest on ₹8000 at 12% per annum for 2 years, compounded annually.","options":"{\"a\":\"2035.20\",\"b\":\"2048.00\",\"c\":\"2056.80\",\"d\":\"2072.00\"}","correct_option":"a","solution_text":"$A = P(1 + \\dfrac{R}{100})^n = 8000(1 + \\dfrac{12}{100})^2 = 8000 \\times 1.2544 = 10035.20$. CI = 10035.20 - 8000 = 2035.20","exam_metadata":"CAT 2023 Slot 3","admin_tags":"[\"Compound Interest\",\"Annual Compounding\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Compound Interest","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"The difference between compound interest and simple interest on a sum of money for 2 years at 10% per annum is ₹100. Find the principal.","options":"{\"a\":\"8000\",\"b\":\"9000\",\"c\":\"10000\",\"d\":\"11000\"}","correct_option":"c","solution_text":"Difference = $P(\\dfrac{R}{100})^2 = P(\\dfrac{10}{100})^2 = P \\times 0.01 = 100$. Therefore, $P = \\dfrac{100}{0.01} = 10000$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Compound Interest\",\"Difference between CI and SI\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Time and Work","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"A can complete a work in 12 days and B can complete the same work in 18 days. In how many days will they complete the work if they work together?","options":"{\"a\":\"6.5 days\",\"b\":\"7.2 days\",\"c\":\"7.5 days\",\"d\":\"8 days\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"A's 1 day work = $\\dfrac{1}{12}$, B's 1 day work = $\\dfrac{1}{18}$. Together: $\\dfrac{1}{12} + \\dfrac{1}{18} = \\dfrac{3+2}{36} = \\dfrac{5}{36}$. Time = $\\dfrac{36}{5} = 7.2$ days","exam_metadata":"CAT 2021 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Time and Work\",\"Working Together\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Time and Work","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"A pipe can fill a tank in 6 hours and another pipe can empty it in 8 hours. If both pipes are opened together, in how many hours will the tank be filled?","options":"{\"a\":\"12 hours\",\"b\":\"18 hours\",\"c\":\"24 hours\",\"d\":\"30 hours\"}","correct_option":"c","solution_text":"Filling pipe: $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ per hour, Emptying pipe: $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ per hour. Net filling: $\\dfrac{1}{6} - \\dfrac{1}{8} = \\dfrac{4-3}{24} = \\dfrac{1}{24}$ per hour. Time = 24 hours","exam_metadata":"CAT 2020 Slot 3","admin_tags":"[\"Time and Work\",\"Pipe and Cistern\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Time, Speed and Distance","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"A train 150m long crosses a platform 250m long in 20 seconds. Find the speed of the train.","options":"{\"a\":\"54 km/h\",\"b\":\"60 km/h\",\"c\":\"72 km/h\",\"d\":\"80 km/h\"}","correct_option":"c","solution_text":"Total distance = 150 + 250 = 400m. Time = 20s. Speed = $\\dfrac{400}{20} = 20$ m/s = $20 \\times \\dfrac{18}{5} = 72$ km/h","exam_metadata":"CAT 2023 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Time Speed Distance\",\"Train and Platform\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Time, Speed and Distance","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"Two trains of lengths 200m and 300m are running in the same direction at speeds of 60 km/h and 40 km/h respectively. In how much time will the faster train overtake the slower train?","options":"{\"a\":\"90 seconds\",\"b\":\"100 seconds\",\"c\":\"120 seconds\",\"d\":\"150 seconds\"}","correct_option":"a","solution_text":"Relative speed = 60 - 40 = 20 km/h = $20 \\times \\dfrac{5}{18} = \\dfrac{50}{9}$ m/s. Distance to cover = 200 + 300 = 500m. Time = $\\dfrac{500}{\\dfrac{50}{9}} = 90$ seconds","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 3","admin_tags":"[\"Time Speed Distance\",\"Relative Speed\",\"Overtaking\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Ratio and Proportion","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"The ratio of ages of A and B is 3:5. If the sum of their ages is 48 years, find the age of A.","options":"{\"a\":\"15 years\",\"b\":\"18 years\",\"c\":\"20 years\",\"d\":\"24 years\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Let ages be 3x and 5x. 3x + 5x = 48, so 8x = 48, x = 6. Age of A = 3x = 3 × 6 = 18 years","exam_metadata":"CAT 2021 Slot 3","admin_tags":"[\"Ratio and Proportion\",\"Age Problems\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Ratio and Proportion","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"If 2A = 3B = 4C, then A:B:C is equal to:","options":"{\"a\":\"6:4:3\",\"b\":\"4:3:2\",\"c\":\"3:2:1\",\"d\":\"2:3:4\"}","correct_option":"a","solution_text":"Let 2A = 3B = 4C = 12k. Then A = 6k, B = 4k, C = 3k. Therefore, A:B:C = 6k:4k:3k = 6:4:3","exam_metadata":"CAT 2020 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Ratio and Proportion\",\"Equal Ratios\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Average","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"The average of 5 numbers is 20. If one number is excluded, the average becomes 18. Find the excluded number.","options":"{\"a\":\"22\",\"b\":\"24\",\"c\":\"26\",\"d\":\"28\"}","correct_option":"d","solution_text":"Sum of 5 numbers = 5 × 20 = 100. Sum of 4 numbers = 4 × 18 = 72. Excluded number = 100 - 72 = 28","exam_metadata":"CAT 2023 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Average\",\"Exclusion of Numbers\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Average","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"The average weight of 8 students is 45 kg. If the weight of the teacher is also included, the average becomes 47 kg. Find the weight of the teacher.","options":"{\"a\":\"61 kg\",\"b\":\"63 kg\",\"c\":\"65 kg\",\"d\":\"67 kg\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Total weight of 8 students = 8 × 45 = 360 kg. Total weight including teacher = 9 × 47 = 423 kg. Teacher's weight = 423 - 360 = 63 kg","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Average\",\"Inclusion of Numbers\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Number System","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"Find the remainder when 2^100 is divided by 7.","options":"{\"a\":\"1\",\"b\":\"2\",\"c\":\"3\",\"d\":\"4\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Using Fermat's Little Theorem: $2^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$. $2^{100} = 2^{96} \\times 2^4 = (2^6)^{16} \\times 2^4 \\equiv 1^{16} \\times 16 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$","exam_metadata":"CAT 2021 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Number System\",\"Remainders\",\"Fermat's Little Theorem\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Number System","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"What is the sum of all two-digit numbers that leave remainder 3 when divided by 7?","options":"{\"a\":\"676\",\"b\":\"702\",\"c\":\"728\",\"d\":\"754\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Two-digit numbers leaving remainder 3 when divided by 7: 10, 17, 24, 31, 38, 45, 52, 59, 66, 73, 80, 87, 94. Sum = $\\dfrac{13}{2}(10 + 94) = \\dfrac{13 \\times 104}{2} = 676$. Wait, let me recalculate: 10+17+24+31+38+45+52+59+66+73+80+87+94 = 702","exam_metadata":"CAT 2020 Slot 2","admin_tags":"[\"Number System\",\"Arithmetic Progression\",\"Remainders\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Geometry","question_number_in_book":1,"question_text":"In a right-angled triangle, the hypotenuse is 13 cm and one side is 5 cm. Find the area of the triangle.","options":"{\"a\":\"24 cm²\",\"b\":\"30 cm²\",\"c\":\"36 cm²\",\"d\":\"42 cm²\"}","correct_option":"b","solution_text":"Using Pythagoras theorem: $13^2 = 5^2 + b^2$, so $169 = 25 + b^2$, $b^2 = 144$, $b = 12$ cm. Area = $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 12 = 30$ cm²","exam_metadata":"CAT 2023 Slot 3","admin_tags":"[\"Geometry\",\"Right Triangle\",\"Pythagoras Theorem\"]"},{"book_source":"Pinnacle 6800 6th Ed","chapter_name":"Geometry","question_number_in_book":2,"question_text":"The radius of a circle is 7 cm. Find the area of the sector subtending an angle of 60° at the center.","options":"{\"a\":\"$\\\\dfrac{77}{3}$ cm²\",\"b\":\"$\\\\dfrac{154}{3}$ cm²\",\"c\":\"$\\\\dfrac{231}{3}$ cm²\",\"d\":\"$\\\\dfrac{308}{3}$ cm²\"}","correct_option":"a","solution_text":"Area of sector = $\\dfrac{\\theta}{360°} \\times \\pi r^2 = \\dfrac{60°}{360°} \\times \\pi \\times 7^2 = \\dfrac{1}{6} \\times \\pi \\times 49 = \\dfrac{49\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{49 \\times 22}{6 \\times 7} = \\dfrac{77}{3}$ cm²","exam_metadata":"CAT 2022 Slot 1","admin_tags":"[\"Geometry\",\"Circle\",\"Sector Area\"]"}]PAR1